<install>
  <update file="${package.root}/install/bundles" todir="${env.bundles}" />
  <copy dir="${package.root}/web" todir="${env.server.home}/nxserver" overwrite="true" />
  <!--
    The package installs no configuration file. Configuration is contributed by Marketplace
    packages to the org.nuxeo.agentic.ui.config extension point and served by a servlet at
    /nuxeo/agentic-ui-config/ (NXSAT-312). Our defaults are a contribution inside the
    nuxeo-agentic-core bundle; a customer ships their own package that depends on this one.
    Nothing is edited on the server and nothing is read from the repository.

    `review-guardrails.mjs` (checkInstallerOwnsNoCustomerFile) fails the gate on any copy into
    agentic-ui-config, which the servlet owns, and on any copy not declared overwrite="true":
    Nuxeo's default is false, and a copy that refuses to overwrite fails the upgrade on the first
    file someone edited, leaving no version installed (NXSAT-317).
  -->
</install>
